    "context": "Six native legacy scheduling syscalls; 5476 checks per architecture: 4600 kernel-facing/state checks and 876 exact pinned musl legacy process-wrapper ENOSYS refusals. Raw low/high words, priority-bound libc calls, guarded buffers and observed policy/priority after errors. Original2460 failures, error-only1308, decoded/reference0; identical native ELF/C on all phases and Linux6.12.51. Two credential cohorts200 cycles retain all slabs/large pages flat. Six isolated production builds, full generated C scope, unchanged allocation allowance failures, compiler/source/ELF pins, five-case final native profile and independent lifetime review. Small scheduler QoS passes x86; original/decoded ARM both fail CPU1 affinity in boots without a device tree. Setup and policy7/SCHED_EXT oracle assumptions remain separate diagnostics. Realtime/deadline, reset/capability/limit rules, SCHED_EXT, target races, namespace/pledge, RR/attribute/affinity argument ABIs, glibc, translation/ELF32 and broad gates remain open.",
